[
  {
    "sha": "d5fe0af0158cbcac7708f653fe44b7df8c967162",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGQ1ZmUwYWYwMTU4Y2JjYWM3NzA4ZjY1M2ZlNDRiN2RmOGM5NjcxNjI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T22:29:45Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T22:29:45Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(gcode): the Klartext reader reads RND, CHF and polar LP / CP\n\nThird slice of the HEIDENHAIN Klartext reader:\n- RND (rounding arc) and CHF (chamfer) between two straight feed lines\n  (L or LP) in the working plane, by one-block look-ahead: the line\n  before waits, the line after sets the cut-back points. The F of the\n  transition acts only on it.\n- LP with PR/PA and IPR/IPA about the pole CC.\n- CP with PA or IPA and DR, with Z/IZ as a helix, split into pieces of\n  at most 90 degrees.\nTransitions next to arcs, FMAX lines, Z changes or block-end M\nfunctions, a CP IPA/DR sign mismatch and polar angles at the pole are\nrefused by name and line. RL/RR, APPR/DEP, CTP, LBL and inch programs\nstay refused.\n\nRefs #2227\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "30465c3a53c2317a5853009434fdea6f91be7292",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/30465c3a53c2317a5853009434fdea6f91be7292"
